            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative haemodynamic studies with mexiletine and lidocaine in patients with coronary heart disease after aorto-coronary bypass (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In two patient groups undergoing coronary surgery (n = 10) hemodynamic side effects of mexiletine and lidocaine were investigated. Changes of clinical importance were seen in cardiac-output, stroke volume, total peripheral resistance, triple- and cardiac index. There are significant differences 10, 15, and 30 min after application (p less than 0.05; p less than 0.025) in cardiac-index.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
